I started a game in wizard mode (as a samurai, if it matters). I wished
for a blessed lockpick and a large box. I applied the lockpick to the
box. A poisoned needle came out of the box, but it missed me. Then, I
applied the lockpick to the box nonstop until turn 600. As expected, my
dexterity increased (from 17 to 18). However, my wisdom also increased
(from 8 to 9). How is this possible?

Also, I once had my wisdom go down at the 600th turn (during normal,
non-wizard mode gameplay), and the only thing I did that could have
abused my wisdom (according to
http://www.geocities.com/dcorbett42/nethack/exercise.htm) was eating a
fortune cookie. This is slightly less strange, because I didn't
experience it in a highly controlled environment, like in the first
example, but it's still extremely strange. Ideas?



